<title>UK: INTERVIEW - No new Penguin charge at Pearson.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - No new Penguin charge at Pearson.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pearson Plc is confident that it will not have to increase the 100 million stg provision it has made to cover the cost of improper accounting at Penguin USA, finance director John Makinson said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are comfortable with that provision,&quot; Makinson told Reuters in a telephone interview. &quot;The 100 million pounds is to cover all known and foreseen eventualities,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
